          %p Noncommutative algebraic geometry studies objects much more general than a single algebra: one wants to glue algebras to more general “systems”. This idea has been around from 1980-s. Of course, one needs a good equivalence among systems. One idea is to replace the algebra by a module and glue categories of modules and then look if the categories are equivalent. But the categories of modules loose the track of the Morita equivalence class, which one would like to keep. For example, one wants to define morphisms between such systems as some class of geometric morphisms, but when one restricts to algebras one would like to have only morphisms of algebras, not the bimodules corresponding to nonaffine morphisms.
          %p This is nicely achieved in a formalism which significantly refines the standard techniques of gluing via corings sketched in chapter 2 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"}> Alexander Rosenberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"} Maxim Kontsevich
              = succeed "," do
                %em Noncommutative smooth spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://books.google.hr/books?id=1xI6j05m7NUC&lpg=PA85&ots=FEtnAU-ImI&dq=alexander%20rosenberg%20gelfand%20seminar%20kontsevich&hl=en&pg=PA85#v=onepage&q&f=false"} gBooks
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9812158"} math.AG/9812158
          %h4#step_1_category_of_covers STEP 1: Category of Covers
          %p
            Given a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coring"} coring
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi δ
                    %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = (M,\delta^M,\epsilon^M)
            is a comonoid in the category of
            = succeed "-bimodules" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-modules)." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\otimes R^{op}
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,M)
            where
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is an
            = succeed "-coring;" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is faithfully flat as the right
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\otimes_R
            is exact and faithful functor. The morphisms
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R_1,M_1)\to (R_2,M_2)
            are given by pairs of algebraic maps in opposite direction, i.e. an algebra map
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_R : R_2\to R_1
            and a bimodule map
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi M
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_M:M_2\to M_1
            satisfying the obvious compatibility conditions with the rest of the structure. This defines the category of covers,
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cover
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cover_k
          %p
            One also defines the category of quasicoherent modules
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QCoh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QCoh(R,M)
            as the category of left
            = succeed "-comodules," do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            together with the coaction
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to M\otimes_R X
          %h4#step_2_introducing_structure_morphism_
            STEP 2: Introducing structure morphism
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_C
          %p
            The objects of the category of “space covers”
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Cover
                    %mi k
                    %mi sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cover_k^{sp}
            is the category of pairs
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,s_C)
            where
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi δ
                    %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = (R,M) = (R,M,\delta^M,\epsilon^M)
            is a cover and
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi k
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^C: R\otimes_k R\to M
            is a surjective homomorphism of coalgebras in the category of
            = succeed "-bimodules." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Cover
                    %mi k
                    %mi sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cover_k^{sp}
            are the morphisms in
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Cover
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cover_k
            compatible with “structure morphisms”
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^C
          %h4#step_3_equivalence_relation_for_the_morphisms STEP 3: Equivalence relation for the morphisms
          %p
            Still some morphisms induce the same inverse image functors for
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QCoh
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QCoh
            categories. To eliminate this, one calls two morphisms
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:(C,s_C)\to (C',s_{C'})
            equivalent if for any element
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi α
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u = \sum x_\alpha\otimes y_\alpha
            in
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ker(s_C)
            the tensor product
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f\otimes g)(u) = 0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g\otimes f)(u)=0
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mover
                      %mi Cover
                      %mo ˜
                    %mi k
                    %mi sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{Cover}^{sp}_k
          %h4#step_4_localizing_on_refinements STEP 4: Localizing on refinements
          %p
            Any cover
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,M)
            in
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Cover
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cover_k
            together with a monomorphism of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\hookrightarrow S
            induces a cover
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,S\otimes_R M\otimes_R S)
            together with a canonical morphism
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,S\otimes_R M\otimes S)\to (R,M)
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cover
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cover_k
            = succeed ";" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cover
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ref
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cover_k[Ref^{-1}]
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_48.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,S\otimes_R M\otimes S)
            can be canonically equipped with a structure morphism and we can in this vain obtain the category of noncommutative spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_49.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi NSpace
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mover
                        %mi Cover
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi k
                      %mi sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ref
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NSpace_k := \tilde{Cover}^{sp}_k[Ref^{-1}]
          %h3#properties Properties
          %p
            Theorem. (AR/MK, sec.2.2) The category of separated quasi-compact schemes over
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_50.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is equivalent to a full subcategory of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_51.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi NSpace
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NSpace_k
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_52.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi k
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg^{op}_k
            is also equivalent to a full subcategory of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_53.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi NSpace
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NSpace_k
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_54.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi NSpace
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NSpace_k
            has finite limits.
          %p
            Theorem. (AR/MK, sec.2.2) Construction
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_55.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi QCoh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B,M)\to QCoh(B,M)
            extends to a functor from the category
            %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_56.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi NSpace
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NSpace_k
            to the category of abelian
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math#mathml_022007287c1a14732e735a6350bb71f44427bdc3_57.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
